WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.922
How can the client improve this process?

2
00:00:03.072 --> 00:00:08.512
Use it when: Operations cases: something is slow, costly or error-prone.

3
00:00:08.562 --> 00:00:13.948
Ask first: Which outcome matters most: cost, speed, capacity or quality?

4
00:00:14.148 --> 00:00:19.718
Map it Steps and hand-offs, time, cost and errors at each step and the bottleneck.

5
00:00:19.768 --> 00:00:23.538
Fix the steps Eliminate, combine, re-order and simplify.

6
00:00:23.588 --> 00:00:27.445
Fix what supports them People and technology and systems.

7
00:00:27.495 --> 00:00:39.450
The slowest step (the bottleneck) sets the output of the whole process. Speeding up any other step adds nothing, so fix the bottleneck first, then check which step becomes the new one.
